    <title>Medications</title>
    <text><table><thead><tr><th>Medication</th><th>Frequency</th><th>Route</th><th>Dates</th><th>Status</th><th>Evidence</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr ID="medication-1"><td>Acetaminophen 300 mg with codeine 30 mg oral tablet, prescribed elsewhere since the crash as one or two tablets every 6 hours as needed, no more than 8 a day; he has been taking 10 to 12 a day</td><td>One or two tablets every 6 hours as needed, no more than 8 a day</td><td>Oral route</td><td>1947-05-04 to 1947-05-11</td><td>completed</td><td>S</td></tr><tr ID="medication-2"><td>Naloxone 4 mg nasal spray, one spray into one nostril for a suspected opioid overdose, repeated every two to three minutes in the other nostril if needed; two-pack dispensed, with instruction for him and his household staff</td><td>One spray as needed for suspected overdose; repeat in 2 to 3 minutes if needed</td><td>Nasal route</td><td>1947-05-04</td><td>active</td><td>S</td></tr><tr ID="medication-3"><td>Buprenorphine 2 mg with naloxone 0.5 mg sublingual film for the first day: 4 mg once withdrawal is moderate (COWS 12 or more), then 2 to 4 mg every one to two hours as needed, to no more than 16 mg on the first day</td><td>First-day induction by the written plan, no more than 16 mg</td><td>Sublingual route</td><td>1947-05-11 to 1947-05-12</td><td>completed</td><td>S</td></tr><tr ID="medication-5"><td>Acetaminophen 500 mg oral tablet, two tablets three times daily (3,000 mg a day) for pain after the crash, now that codeine combination tablets have stopped</td><td>Two tablets three times daily, no more than 3,000 mg a day</td><td>Oral route</td><td>1947-05-11</td><td>active</td><td>S</td></tr><tr ID="medication-6"><td>Sertraline 50 mg oral tablet, one tablet daily</td><td>One tablet daily</td><td>Oral route</td><td>1947-05-11 to 1947-06-08</td><td>completed</td><td>S</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

